370:  /// is consumed, which is what forces `max_concurrent_windows` down and caps our parallelism at ~7
371:  /// cores (the reference implementation uses ~43). A frame only needs (m/z, intensity, 1/K0) per peak plus one RT, so we
372:  /// store structure-of-arrays with quantised keys and materialise a PeakMap ONLY inside the worker
