   537	### STEP 02 sub-arm 2 RESULT (2026-09-02, 22:49): SAME PRECURSORS, SAME 85% -- the deficit is per-precursor content
   538	Reference: the reference implementation's 700,434 dataset D pseudo-spectra (RT/m/z/z). Of our 1,105,532 precursor hypotheses 445,008 match one
   539	(10 s / 10 ppm / z); emitting only those gives 432,579 spectra.
   540	| dataset D arm | spectra | Sage @1% | MSFragger @1% | MSFragger ratio vs dt |
   560	| the reference implementation-identified / shared / **dt-only** | 14,974 / 11,037 / **3,937** | 14,974 / 11,367 / **3,607** |
   561	| dt-only for which we HAVE a PSM (searched, below threshold) | **2,501 (64%)** | 1,567 (43%) |
   562	| dt-only with NO PSM at all (never emitted or < min_frags) | 1,436 (36%) | 2,040 (57%) |
   563	| dt-only, ours vs dt: hyperscore median | 12.5 vs 16.2 | 13.1 vs 16.2 |
   564	| dt-only, ours vs dt: matched ions median (of 26 theoretical) | **7 vs 9** (deficit +2; p25 +1, p75 +4; same at every charge) | 6 vs 9 (deficit +3) |
   565	| shared, ours vs dt: hyperscore / matched ions | 23.6 vs 22.9 / 12 vs 12 | 24.4 vs 22.4 / 12 vs 12 |
   566	Reading: on the peptides we both find, our spectra are as good as the reference implementation's. On the ~3,900 we miss, two thirds
   567	are searched and fall short by ~2 of ~9 fragment ions -- the faint tail is under-covered: the weaker fragments of
   568	faint precursors are gated out (`gate:min_correlation` 0.3, `min_correlation_points`) or never traced
   569	(`trace:ms2_noise_threshold_int` 10, `ms2_chrom_peak_snr` 1.0). The remaining third we never emit at all (the MS1
   570	funnel: no hypothesis or < min_frags). This is the first mechanistic, per-peptide account of the MSFragger deficit.
   571	**Pre-registered arms (running next, both engines):** (a) `gate:min_correlation 0.2`, (b) `trace:ms2_noise_threshold_int 5`,
   572	(c) both. Prediction: the dt-only matched-ion deficit shrinks toward 0 and the MSFragger ratio rises above 90%;
   573	falsifier: the deficit stays at +2 (then the missing ions are not in our traces at all -> MS2 aggregation / detector).
