   575	### CONTENT CANDIDATE 1 FALSIFIED (2026-09-03, 01:52): corr_power=2 helps MSFragger too
   576	`-assembly:corr_power 0` on the apex arm: Sage 11,502 (−8.3% vs 12,537; only-cp2 1,640 / only-cp0 605) and
   577	**MSFragger 11,429 (−4.2% vs 11,927)**. The correlation-power intensity reshaping is a win on both engines (first
   578	MSFragger measurement of it; the July +8-10% was Sage-only). Intensity structure is not what MSFragger dislikes in our
   579	faint-tail spectra. Remaining content candidate: fragment coverage (the +2 matched-ion deficit) -- arms running.
   580	
   581	### COVERAGE ARMS FALSIFIED (2026-09-03, 03:10): the missing fragment ions are not in our traces at all
   582	| dataset D arm | spectra | Sage vs apex 12,537 | MSFragger vs apex 11,927 | dt-only: ours vs dt matched ions |
   583	|---|---|---|---|---|
   584	| `gate:min_correlation 0.2` | 928,572 | 12,509 (145/117) | 11,935 | 7 vs 9, deficit +2 |
   585	| `trace:ms2_noise_threshold_int 5` | 927,813 | **12,537, symdiff 0 (byte-identical)** | 11,927 | 7 vs 9, deficit +2 |
   586	| both | 928,572 | 12,509 | 11,935 | 7 vs 9, deficit +2 |
