   588	(the SNR / min-length gates already decide). Per the pre-registered falsifier, the ~2 missing ions per faint spectrum are
   589	not in our fragment TRACES: they are peaks that never become a trace (single-frame or sub-SNR) -- exactly the population
   590	the reference implementation's ~500-peak spectra carry and our ~55-trace spectra do not. Next arm (content candidate 3): backfill each
   591	pseudo-spectrum with the raw picked MS2 peaks of the precursor's apex frame inside its IM band (top-N not already
   592	present), the DIA-Umpire/the reference implementation-style "peak-level" spectrum, both engines; falsifier: dt-only deficit stays +2.
   593	
   594	### CONTENT CANDIDATE 3 -- PRE-REGISTERED (2026-09-03, 03:35): raw apex-frame peak backfill
   595	`SPEXTRACT_BACKFILL_RAW=N` adds to each pseudo-spectrum the N most intense raw picked MS2 peaks of the frame nearest
   596	the precursor's RT, inside its 1/K0 band (delta_im), not already present within 10 ppm -- untraced, single-frame
   597	content (the population the coverage arms showed we never trace). Arms: N=50, N=150. Predictions: if the faint tail's
   598	missing ions are these peaks, the dt-only matched-ion deficit (+2) shrinks and the MSFragger ratio rises (>= 90%);
   599	Sage may fall if the added peaks are noise (the 150-peak search cap protects MSFragger more than Sage). Falsifier:
   600	deficit stays +2 with N=150 -> the missing ions are not in the picked frame either (pick-level / MS2 aggregation).
   601	
   602	### Backfill arm, first run INVALID (2026-09-03, 04:42) -- and the never-searched third attributed
   603	N=50 and N=150 came back byte-identical to apex (Sage symdiff 0, MSFragger 11,927): the backfill never fired because
   604	`detectTraces_` partitions the window's PeakMap into bands and clears it, so the map is empty by assembly time. Fixed
   605	(a retained copy when the arm is on); rerun in flight. Not a result.
   606	**MS1 funnel (funnel_dtonly.py on the apex arm's hypothesis dump, 1,105,532 hypotheses):** of the 1,436 the reference implementation-only
   607	peptides for which we have NO PSM, 654 (46%) have a precursor hypothesis of ours within 10 s / 10 ppm / z (918 = 64%
   608	within 30 s) -> hypothesised but no spectrum reached the search (assembly: < min_frags or no correlated fragments);
   609	~500 (35%) have no hypothesis at all (MS1 trace / envelope). So the 3,937 dt-only peptides split ~64% searched-but-
   610	under-covered / ~17% hypothesised-not-emitted / ~19% never hypothesised.
   611	
   612	### ASSEMBLY-LOSS ARM -- PRE-REGISTERED (2026-09-03, 04:45): `assembly:min_fragments` 2
   613	17% of the the reference implementation-only peptides have a precursor hypothesis of ours but no spectrum reached the search. The gate that
   614	drops a hypothesised precursor at assembly is `assembly:min_fragments` (a spectrum with fewer correlated fragments is
   615	not emitted). Arm: min_fragments 2 (the default is already 3), both engines. Prediction: the dt-only "we have SOME PSM"
   616	fraction rises from 64% and MSFragger gains if those spectra are identifiable; falsifier: the added spectra are
   617	unidentifiable noise (Sage/MSFragger flat or down, emission up). Runs after the backfill rerun (`bench_minfrag.sh`).
   618	
   619	### CONTENT CANDIDATE 3 CONFIRMED (2026-09-03, 05:39): raw apex-frame peak backfill lifts MSFragger to 90% -- at a Sage cost
   620	| dataset D arm | Sage @1% (vs apex 12,537) | MSFragger @1% (vs apex 11,927) | ratio vs dt | shared with dt / dt-only | dt-only matched-ion deficit |
   621	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   622	| apex | 12,537 | 11,927 | 85.6% | 11,037 / 3,937 | +2 |
   623	| **backfill N=50** | 12,208 (−2.6%; 1,215 / 886) | **12,539 (+5.1%)** | **90.0%** | **12,188 / 2,786** | +3 (on the smaller remaining set) |
   624	| backfill N=150 | 11,190 (−10.7%) | 12,042 (+1.0%) | 86.4% | 11,437 / 3,537 | +2 |
